{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "20446",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.9,
      "end_seconds": 4.27,
      "duration_seconds": 3.37,
      "text": "Erm, sorry I'm a little late, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 5.6,
      "end_seconds": 10.45,
      "duration_seconds": 4.85,
      "text": "Yes, come in and sit down. What brings you here today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 11.29,
      "end_seconds": 20.36,
      "duration_seconds": 9.07,
      "text": "Doctor, it's a red, hot area on my lower leg. It's getting on my nerves now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 22.14,
      "end_seconds": 23.73,
      "duration_seconds": 1.59,
      "text": "When did this begin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 26.8,
      "end_seconds": 30.27,
      "duration_seconds": 3.47,
      "text": "Since Monday, that's when it began."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 30.66,
      "end_seconds": 34.97,
      "duration_seconds": 4.31,
      "text": "yes, carry on is there something that settles it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 37.05,
      "end_seconds": 40.71,
      "duration_seconds": 3.66,
      "text": "Oh, I get some relief from elevation."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 46.19,
      "end_seconds": 49.38,
      "duration_seconds": 3.19,
      "text": "Have you had pain in the calf?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 51.27,
      "end_seconds": 58.21,
      "duration_seconds": 6.94,
      "text": "Yes, I have. With pain in the calf, it happens every other day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 59.62,
      "end_seconds": 63.15,
      "duration_seconds": 3.53,
      "text": "time for your numbers, if that's okay"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 76.12,
      "end_seconds": 78.25,
      "duration_seconds": 2.13,
      "text": "Okay, this won't take long..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 89.61,
      "end_seconds": 103.77,
      "duration_seconds": 14.16,
      "text": "okay: BP is 107 over 77, temp 39.4 degrees and BMI works out to 36.6, height 162 centimetres, weight 96 kilos, pulse 94, SpO2 95 percent on room air"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 106.45,
      "end_seconds": 110.13,
      "duration_seconds": 3.68,
      "text": "alright, over here please and I'll take a look"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 111.42,
      "end_seconds": 112.38,
      "duration_seconds": 0.96,
      "text": "That's alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 114.05,
      "end_seconds": 116.43,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "Take a deep breath for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 126.97,
      "end_seconds": 135.55,
      "duration_seconds": 8.58,
      "text": "there is a warm, red, tender patch about ten centimetres across on the right shin with mild swelling"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 141.07,
      "end_seconds": 144.45,
      "duration_seconds": 3.38,
      "text": "That's the examination finished. How about pus?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 149.09,
      "end_seconds": 150.76,
      "duration_seconds": 1.67,
      "text": "No. No pus."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 151.06,
      "end_seconds": 155.57,
      "duration_seconds": 4.51,
      "text": "right, right a few quick ones: breathlessness, vomiting or wound?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 156.86,
      "end_seconds": 158.99,
      "duration_seconds": 2.13,
      "text": "None of those, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 160.91,
      "end_seconds": 163.22,
      "duration_seconds": 2.31,
      "text": "your breathing, any trouble there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 168.31,
      "end_seconds": 169.79,
      "duration_seconds": 1.48,
      "text": "No, nothing there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 171.04,
      "end_seconds": 173.44,
      "duration_seconds": 2.4,
      "text": "tell me about your eating"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 175.54,
      "end_seconds": 180.63,
      "duration_seconds": 5.09,
      "text": "I drink a lot of tea and snack through the day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 181.15,
      "end_seconds": 183.27,
      "duration_seconds": 2.12,
      "text": "is there someone at home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 185.0,
      "end_seconds": 188.85,
      "duration_seconds": 3.85,
      "text": "My husband and I live above the shop."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 196.49,
      "end_seconds": 199.91,
      "duration_seconds": 3.42,
      "text": "did you ever have any procedures done?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 201.79,
      "end_seconds": 207.95,
      "duration_seconds": 6.16,
      "text": "Yes, I had a wisdom tooth extraction under sedation, five years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 209.43,
      "end_seconds": 212.82,
      "duration_seconds": 3.39,
      "text": "has anyone ever diagnosed you with something?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 216.83,
      "end_seconds": 218.02,
      "duration_seconds": 1.19,
      "text": "Yes, diabetes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 219.98,
      "end_seconds": 224.49,
      "duration_seconds": 4.51,
      "text": "Okay, I can see diabetes in your file as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 233.2,
      "end_seconds": 237.76,
      "duration_seconds": 4.56,
      "text": "Any inherited conditions that you know of in the the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 238.62,
      "end_seconds": 240.51,
      "duration_seconds": 1.89,
      "text": "my son has asthma"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 259.21,
      "end_seconds": 263.04,
      "duration_seconds": 3.83,
      "text": "Which medicines do you take at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 264.76,
      "end_seconds": 268.37,
      "duration_seconds": 3.61,
      "text": "It's gliclazide, 80 milligrams, twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 269.43,
      "end_seconds": 276.6,
      "duration_seconds": 7.17,
      "text": "so where does that leave us? It fits best with cellulitis of the right leg"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 277.2,
      "end_seconds": 279.27,
      "duration_seconds": 2.07,
      "text": "Is it dangerous, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 280.77,
      "end_seconds": 312.19,
      "duration_seconds": 31.42,
      "text": "It's reasonable to be concerned, but right now cellulitis of the right leg is my leading thought, not anything worse. I want blood tests done, that's for skin infection. The result will help us decide whether anything more is needed. I'd like you to take flucloxacillin, 500 milligrams, four times a day, for seven days. That should help with cellulitis. Mark the edge of the redness with a pen and keep the leg raised when sitting."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 312.61,
      "end_seconds": 328.01,
      "duration_seconds": 15.4,
      "text": "Sure. Come back or go to emergency straight away if the redness spreads quickly or you get a high fever. Can you tell me the plan back in your own words, so I know I've explained it clearly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 330.03,
      "end_seconds": 337.43,
      "duration_seconds": 7.4,
      "text": "So, I take the the flucloxacillin, 500 milligrams, four times a day. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 337.97,
      "end_seconds": 342.91,
      "duration_seconds": 4.94,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. I think we're done unless you have questions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 344.33,
      "end_seconds": 347.61,
      "duration_seconds": 3.28,
      "text": "Great, thank you for your help."
    }
  ]
}